# Contributing to {{ project_name }}

This repo was initialized with nbis-admin version {{ version }}.

## Development setup

The repo must be under source control:

    git init
    git add -f .
    git commit -m "Initial commit"

Set up the environment with pixi:

    pixi init
    pixi shell

## Managing dependencies

Add Python dependencies to `pyproject.toml`:

    pixi add --pypi <package>       # for PyPI packages
    pixi add <package>              # for conda-forge packages

Prefer conda-forge when the package is available there; fall back to
PyPI otherwise.

## Extending the project

- `nbis-admin add diary` — adds `docs/diary/` for project notes
- `nbis-admin add running-slides` — adds a RevealJS slide template
- `nbis-admin add tool <name>` — scaffold a new CLI tool
- `nbis-admin smk add <name>` — add a Snakemake workflow

See `nbis-admin --help` for the full list.

## Publication

Before publication, clean up the codebase and remove development
documentation. The easiest approach:

    git switch --orphan publication

Then cherry-pick the relevant code from `main`.
